  "id": "COMPOUND:30129 - PROTEIN:5677",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which alpha-Cedrene epoxide may interact with JM1, through a series of molecular targets. The compound is implicated in targeting multiple cell lines, including HuT78, SCCH-26, and LAPC4, all of which are known to be targets of 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide, a compound that itself has a known target of JM1. This indicates a possible pathway where alpha-Cedrene epoxide may act through a shared intermediate, 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide, to influence JM1. The evidence is supported by a consistent pattern across three distinct pathways, each linking alpha-Cedrene epoxide to JM1 via a common intermediate. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between alpha-Cedrene epoxide and JM1. The mechanism appears to involve a regulatory pathway that could be relevant in the context of cancer or other diseases, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
